      "title": "An IRA is an individual tax arrangement",
      "narration": "Marcus wants to save part of his earnings in a traditional individual retirement arrangement, usually called an I R A. It can be established through an eligible financial institution, including an insurance company. The account is individually owned, even when spouses use a joint tax return. Eligibility for a regular contribution generally requires qualifying compensation, such as wages or net self-employment income. A pension check or investment interest is not automatically that compensation. There is no upper age cutoff for regular contributions under current law, but the other requirements remain. A spousal contribution can be possible on a joint return using qualifying combined compensation; it still goes into a separate individual arrangement.",
