      "narration": "Consider an owner who turns seventy-three during twenty twenty-six. The first traditional I R A required minimum distribution is for that year and generally must be taken by April first of twenty twenty-seven. The next year's required distribution is due by December thirty-first of twenty twenty-seven, so delaying the first payment can put both in one tax year. Continuing to work does not postpone this traditional account requirement. Use the applicable birth-year rule rather than memorizing age seventy and one half from old material. Current law also schedules age seventy-five for younger cohorts. A required minimum distribution is a minimum withdrawal requirement, not an instruction to surrender every annuity or spend the entire account.",
