      "title": "Inherited arrangements need classification",
      "text": "Eligible designated beneficiaries include a surviving spouse, the owner’s minor child, a qualifying disabled or chronically ill individual, or an individual no more than ten years younger than the owner. Other designated individuals commonly face the ten-year rule. When the owner dies before the required beginning date and that rule applies, no annual distribution is generally required before the final year. When the owner dies on or after that date, annual distributions generally apply as well. Estate and qualifying trust rules differ.",
